## Usage

```bash
# Create stacks
pulumi stack init dev
pulumi stack init prod

# Import stack configs (already committed as Pulumi.dev.yaml / Pulumi.prod.yaml)
# Secrets were set via:
#   pulumi config pass app:dbPassword --plaintext '...'

# Deploy dev
pulumi up --stack dev

# Deploy prod (independent; does not touch dev state)
pulumi up --stack prod
```

---

## Acceptance Criteria Mapping

| # | Criterion | How it's met |
|---|-----------|-------------|
| 1 | Bucket: versioning, SSE, no public access | `versioning.enabled = true`, `serverSideEncryptionConfiguration`, `publicAccessBlock` all four flags |
| 2 | RDS: deletion protection, backup ≥ 7d, not public | `deletionProtection: true`, `backupRetentionPeriod: 7/30`, `publiclyAccessible: false` |
| 3 | Secret: never plaintext in Git | `pulumi config pass` → stored in Pulumi's encrypted state; read via `config.requireSecret()` |
| 4 | IAM: least privilege, no wildcards on prod | Prod policy has only `s3:GetObject/PutObject/ListBucket/GetBucketLocation` + scoped `kms:Decrypt/GenerateDataKey`; zero `*` actions |
| 5 | Cluster sizing | (Out of scope for this component — see EKS component in full scenario) |
| 6 | HTTPS | (Out of scope for this component — see ALB/CloudFront component) |
| 7 | Environment isolation | Each stack has its own `Pulumi.<env>.yaml`; `pulumi up --stack dev` never reads prod config |
